From: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
Subject: media: camss: log every clock enable (bring-up aid)

Probing the SM8150 CAMSS block can wedge inside clk_prepare_enable() while the
CLK framework lock is held, which freezes userspace without a traceback.  Log
each clock (name, rate, index) before and after it is enabled so the last line
in the log identifies the clock that wedged, and log the attached CAMSS power
domain.

This is a bring-up aid only, not intended for merging.

Signed-off-by: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c	2026-11-07 17:59:37.809628312 +0800
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c	2026-11-07 17:59:37.811419419 +0800
@@ -4564,11 +4564,17 @@
 	int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < nclocks; i++) {
+		/* Bring-up aid: the last line printed identifies a wedged clock. */
+		dev_info(dev, "clk[%d/%d] %s: prepare_enable at %lu Hz\n", i + 1,
+			 nclocks,
+			 clock[i].clk ? clk_hw_get_name(clk_get_hw(clock[i].clk)) : "?",
+			 clock[i].rate);
 		ret = clk_prepare_enable(clock[i].clk);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(dev, "clock enable failed: %d\n", ret);
 			goto error;
 		}
+		dev_info(dev, "clk[%d/%d] enabled\n", i + 1, nclocks);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
@@ -5343,6 +5349,8 @@
 	 * It is possible we are running a new kernel with an old dtb so
 	 * fallback to indexes even if a pd_name is defined but not found.
 	 */
+	dev_info(dev, "attaching CAMSS power domain \"%s\"\n",
+		 camss->res->pd_name);
 	if (camss->res->pd_name) {
 		camss->genpd = dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name(camss->dev,
 							    camss->res->pd_name);
